<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basic Law for the Federal Republic of Germany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949</span> · Also known as Grundgesetz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Basic Law for the Federal Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> is the German constitution, drafted by a parliamentary council of the western states and in force from 23 May 1949. Intended as provisional until reunification, it set up a federal parliamentary democracy with strong basic rights and a constitutional court. It became the constitution of all Germany in 1990. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>'s Landtag rejected it but accepted its validity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basic-law-for-the-federal-republic-of-germany.jpg" alt="Basic Law for the Federal Republic of Germany" width="255" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: bpb.de · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grundgesetz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
